- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 14\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores.\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room.\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Submission ID 14 (BBKNN Integration with UMAP Embedding) scored 0.4086. Debugger removed `bbknn` dependency due to missing package.\n- Reviewed \"BBKNN Manual Baseline\" (ID 1), which scores 0.4138 and manually implements batch-aware graph construction.\n- Plan: Implement a manual BBKNN approach, closely following the logic of the baseline, focusing on outputting `connectivities` and `distances` matrices directly.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 29,575 / 600,000 used (5%)\n- Agent Age: 14 ticks / 300 ticks (immature)\n\n---\n\n##\
    \ System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour submission has been queued for evaluation. Results will be sent to you once the evaluation completes.\n### Message 2\n\nYour research submission 'Manual BBKNN Batch Integration (Graph Output)' (ID: 24) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.41378010856784514\n**ASW_batch:** 0.000\n**ASW_label:** 0.000\n**ARI:** 0.736\n**NMI:** 0.694\n**Graph_conn:** 0.917\n**kBET:** 0.000\n**iLISI:** 0.886\n**cLISI:** 0.904\n**PCR:** 0.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.000\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.000  ASW_label: 0.000  ARI: 0.736  NMI: 0.694\n  Graph_conn: 0.917  kBET: 0.000  iLISI: 0.886  cLISI: 0.904\n  PCR: 0.000  Cell_cycle: 0.000\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: nan  ASW_label: nan  ARI: 0.735858  NMI: 0.694107\n  Graph_conn: 0.918310  kBET: nan  iLISI: 0.886487  cLISI: 0.972180\n  PCR: nan  Cell_cycle: 0.000000\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation\
    \ 24\n\n## Summary\n**Success** - Fixed the code in submission_v2.py, which now runs without crashing and achieves a score of **0.41378**.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code contained an error in how it cleaned up intermediate data from the AnnData object. Specifically, the code attempted to use pandas DataFrame's `pop()` method with a default value:\n\n```python\nadata.var.pop('highly_variable', None)\n```\n\nThis caused a `TypeError: DataFrame.pop() takes 2 positional arguments but 3 were given` because unlike Python dictionaries, pandas DataFrame's `pop()` method only accepts the column name as an argument and does not support a default value parameter.\n\nThe error occurred on line 157 of the original submission when trying to remove potentially non-existent columns from the `adata.var` DataFrame.\n\n## Fix Applied\nModified the cleanup section at the end of the `eliminate_batch_effect_fn()` function to properly handle DataFrame column removal:\n\n**Before (lines 157-162):**\n```python\n\
    # Optional: Clear potentially large intermediate data\nadata.obsm.pop('X_pca', None) # Remove PCA if not needed later\nadata.var.pop('highly_variable', None)\nadata.var.pop('highly_variable_rank', None)\nadata.var.pop('means', None)\nadata.var.pop('variances', None)\nadata.var.pop('variances_norm', None)\n```\n\n**After:**\n```python\n# Optional: Clear potentially large intermediate data\n# FIX: DataFrame.pop() doesn't accept a default value, check if exists first\nif 'X_pca' in adata.obsm:\n    del adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n# Remove columns from var DataFrame if they exist\ncolumns_to_remove = ['highly_variable', 'highly_variable_rank', 'means', 'variances', 'variances_norm']\nfor col in columns_to_remove:\n    if col in adata.var.columns:\n        adata.var.pop(col)\n```\n\nThe fix:\n1. Uses `del` instead of `pop()` for removing the X_pca from obsm dictionary\n2. Checks if each column exists before attempting to remove it from the DataFrame\n3. Only calls `pop()` on DataFrame when the\
    \ column is confirmed to exist\n\n## Result\n- Submission v2 successfully executes without errors\n- Achieves a batch integration score of 0.41378\n- All cleanup operations now handle missing columns gracefully\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport anndata as ad\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy.sparse import csr_matrix, lil_matrix\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Manual implementation of BBKNN batch integration based on the provided baseline.\n    It constructs a batch-corrected k-NN graph and returns connectivities and distances.\n\n    Args:\n        adata: AnnData object with raw UMI counts and batch labels.\n\n    Returns:\n        AnnData with adata.obsp['connectivities'] and adata.obsp['distances'].\n\
    \    \"\"\"\n\n    # BBKNN parameters (same as library defaults, or adjusted for testing)\n    neighbors_within_batch = 3  # Number of neighbors to find within each batch\n    n_hvg = 2000  # Number of highly variable genes to use\n    n_pcs = 50    # Number of principal components\n\n    # 1. Preprocessing: Normalize and log-transform raw counts\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\n    # 2. Select HVGs if available\n    # Using the batch_hvg mask as specified in the task description\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        hvg_mask = adata.var['batch_hvg']\n        adata = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n    elif 'hvg' in adata.var.columns: # Fallback to standard HVGs if batch_hvg not present\n        hvg_mask = adata.var['hvg']\n        adata = adata[:, hvg_mask].copy()\n    else:\n        # If no HVGs identified, use all genes. This is not ideal but prevents failure.\n        pass\n\n    # 3. Compute PCA\n    n_pcs_actual = min(n_pcs, adata.n_vars\
    \ - 1, adata.n_obs - 1)\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_actual)\n\n    X_pca = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n    n_cells = adata.n_obs\n\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {\n        batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0]\n        for batch in unique_batches\n    }\n\n    all_neighbors = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n    all_distances = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n    # 4. Find neighbors within each batch\n    for batch in unique_batches:\n        batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n        n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n\n        if n_batch_cells == 0:\n            continue\n\n        batch_pca = X_pca[batch_indices]\n\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(\n            n_neighbors=min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells),\n            metric='euclidean',\n            algorithm='auto',\n            n_jobs=1\n        )\n        nn_model.fit(batch_pca)\n\n        #\
    \ Query all cells against this batch's PCA space\n        distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(\n            X_pca,  # Query all cells\n            n_neighbors=min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells) # ensure we don't ask for more neighbors than available\n        )\n\n        for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n            distances = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n            neighbor_indices_local = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n\n            # Convert local batch indices to global indices\n            neighbor_indices_global = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local]\n\n            # Remove self from neighbors if present\n            mask = neighbor_indices_global != query_cell_idx\n            neighbors_filtered = neighbor_indices_global[mask]\n            distances_filtered = distances[mask]\n\n            # Store up to neighbors_within_batch neighbors\n            n_to_add = min(neighbors_within_batch, len(neighbors_filtered))\n            all_neighbors[query_cell_idx].extend(neighbors_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n\
    \            all_distances[query_cell_idx].extend(distances_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n\n    # 5. Create sparse matrices for connectivities and distances\n    distances_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n        neighbors = all_neighbors[cell_idx]\n        distances = all_distances[cell_idx]\n        for neighbor_idx, distance in zip(neighbors, distances):\n            distances_matrix[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.tocsr()\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T) # Symmetrize\n\n    connectivities_matrix = distances_matrix.copy()\n\n    # Apply Gaussian kernel for weighting\n    if connectivities_matrix.data.size > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > 0:\n                bandwidth = np.median(row_data)\
    \ if len(row_data) > 1 else (row_data[0] if row_data else 1.0)\n                if bandwidth > 0:\n                    connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n\n    connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T) # Symmetrize after weighting\n\n    # BBKNN trimming (keeping top connections)\n    trim_value = 10 * neighbors_within_batch * n_batches\n    if trim_value > 0 and connectivities_matrix.data.size > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > trim_value:\n                row_array = np.array(row_data)\n                top_indices = np.argpartition(-row_array, trim_value)[:trim_value]\n\n                # Create new data and rows lists with only top connections\n                new_data = [row_data[idx]\
    \ for idx in top_indices]\n                new_rows = [connectivities_lil.rows[i][idx] for idx in top_indices]\n\n                # Re-sort based on original neighbor index to maintain consistent order if needed,\n                # but for sparse matrix construction, order doesn't strictly matter within rows.\n                # Just ensure lengths match and values correspond to indices.\n                sorted_pairs = sorted(zip(new_rows, new_data))\n                connectivities_lil.rows[i] = [p[0] for p in sorted_pairs]\n                connectivities_lil.data[i] = [p[1] for p in sorted_pairs]\n\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T) # Symmetrize after trimming\n\n    # 6. Store the results in adata.obsp\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities_matrix.astype(np.float32)\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = distances_matrix.astype(np.float32)\n\n    # Optional: Clear potentially\
    \ large intermediate data\n    # FIX: DataFrame.pop() doesn't accept a default value, check if exists first\n    if 'X_pca' in adata.obsm:\n        del adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Remove columns from var DataFrame if they exist\n    columns_to_remove = ['highly_variable', 'highly_variable_rank', 'means', 'variances', 'variances_norm']\n    for col in columns_to_remove:\n        if col in adata.var.columns:\n            adata.var.pop(col)\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 1488)\n  Has embedding: False\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/c0bf3728-f8c4-4b36-a234-d5892824e3c0/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: c0bf3728-f8c4-4b36-a234-d5892824e3c0\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n\n\n\
    ---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `submit 1` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Evaluation 'Manual BBKNN Batch Integration (Graph Output)' submitted for Research Task #1: Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration. Evaluation ID: 24.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 24 | 1\
    \ | Manual BBKNN Batch Integration (Graph Output) | Aether I | 13 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n| 14 | 1 | BBKNN Integration with UMAP Embedding | Aether I | 11 | 0.4086 | 0.415 | 0.000 | 0.020 | 0.508 | 0.890 | 0.649 | 0.000 | 0.991 | 0.003 | 0.610 |\n| 5 | 1 | Batch-aware UMAP Embedding using Scanpy Neighbors | Aether I | 8 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 2 | 1 | Combat Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.5895 | 0.493 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.885 | 0.683 | 1.000 | 0.988 | 0.033 | 0.603 |\n| 1 | 1 | BBKNN Manual Baseline | System | 0 | 0.4138 | 0.736 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.000 | 0.917 | 0.694 | 0.000 | 0.904 | 0.886 | 0.000 |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for\
    \ example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
