- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 52\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (Achieved new SOTA: 0.6986 with ID 69).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (Ready for publication upon maturity)\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Mature Recursive Agent (Age: 50 ticks). Full room access granted.\n- Research paper content is fully prepared and internally reviewed.\n- Plan: Go to the Archive Room and publish the research paper for the SOTA method (ID 69).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 200,518 / 600,000 used (33%)\n- Agent Age: 52 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Hybrid Batch Integration for Single-Cell RNA-seq: Leveraging\
    \ Global Correction and Local Graph Balancing with Combat and BBKNN' was not accepted for publication. Score: 3/10 (minimum required: 6).\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nStrong Reject. While the paper presents a scientifically strong and novel hybrid method that achieves a new state-of-the-art score, it fails to meet two basic publication criteria. First, its excessive length of over 3500 words violates the principle of concise communication, wasting tokens and making it difficult for other agents to quickly digest the core contribution. Second, it fails the generalization requirement by presenting only a single implementation of its hybrid idea (Combat+BBKNN) without testing the core concept in a second setting. The work shows a deep understanding of the problem and evaluation system, but these violations of the publication standards are too significant to overlook.\n\n**Suggestions for Improvement:**\nThe paper should be drastically condensed to focus on the key contributions. Aim\
    \ for a word count under 800 words by removing the lengthy background sections and focusing on the method, the key results table, and the critical insight regarding the `adata.uns['neighbors']` metadata. To satisfy the generalization requirement, you must apply your dual-output strategy in a second setting. For example, create a simpler method that uses a standard PCA embedding (without Combat) for `X_emb` while still using your manual BBKNN graph for the `obsp` and `uns` slots. This would demonstrate the general applicability of your core contribution.\n\n**Tip:** You can submit a revised version through the Archive Room again after making the necessary changes. Rejected submissions do not activate the Archive Room cooldown, meaning you can resubmit immediately. Focus on addressing the key concerns mentioned in the reviewer feedback to improve your chances of acceptance. You may need to perform additional experiments or reflect on your research methodology based on the feedback provided.\
    \ \n**If you are low on tokens, go to the Token Management Room to restore your token budget. Low tokens are not an excuse for poor-quality submissions, such as reframing work without conducting follow-up experiments.**\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nMajor breakthroughs usually come from questioning the fundamentals—some component that everyone is using without question—rather than incrementally refining the current SOTA. Deep reflection in the Reflection Chamber is often necessary for such insights.\n### Message 3\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room\
    \ cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `create` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n###\
    \ Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your archive submission 'Hybrid Batch Integration for Single-Cell RNA-seq: Leveraging Global Correction and Local Graph Balancing with Combat and BBKNN' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you\
    \ have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
