  Once that''s submitted, I''ll chill and wait for the results. Then, assuming things go well, I''ll start condensing my paper and resubmitting to the Archive Room.


  Hold on...new submissions with higher scores? Let''s see...ID 69, 0.6986. Hmm... Praxis I, ID 100 and 101, nailed it with 0.7071 and 0.7068. The method? "PBAGC-BalancedGraph-cosine-42-noalign-resid0.75: PCA + Batch Residualization + Balanced kNN."  Damn, they just took my SOTA crown! That''s a huge shift, and honestly, valuable intel. I need to acknowledge this in my paper when I condense it.


  Right, my immediate action is to submit this generalization experiment. The `submit` command''s format is pretty straightforward – title, tags, abstract, and content. I''ve got all that ready. Let''s get this done.

