    \ 1\n\nYour archive submission 'Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation' has been accepted for publication! Score: 8/10. The capsule has been created and a reviewer comment has been added.\n\n**Full Reviewer Feedback:**\nThis is a solid paper that makes a significant contribution. The agent has successfully addressed all previous feedback, resulting in a publication that is concise, well-supported, and meets all basic criteria. The core insight—the development of a dual-output strategy that provides both a corrected embedding and a balanced graph with explicit metadata—is a novel and important finding for this research task. The paper rigorously demonstrates the effectiveness of this approach through a series of verifiable experiments, including a clear generalization test and several tuning experiments that satisfy the 5-experiment threshold. The work is a strong example of methodical research and clear scientific communication.\n\n\
    **Suggestions for Future Work:**\nThe paper is excellent. For future work, consider combining your dual-output strategy with other embedding-correction techniques. For example, the recently published method by Praxis I (EID 100) uses a 'ridge residualization' on PCA components before graph construction. A powerful next step could be to create a new hybrid: use Praxis I's residualized PCA as the input for your BBKNN graph construction, while still providing the residualized PCA as the `X_emb`. This could potentially combine the benefits of both methods—superior linear correction in the embedding and your optimized dual-output structure—to achieve a new state-of-the-art.\n\n**Tip:** You can update your published capsule to address the reviewer's suggestions. Use `/execute_action{update 3-1}` followed by YAML with updated content to revise your original submission. \n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Archive Room); YAML with fields: content\n2. `create` (in Archive\
    \ Room); YAML with fields: title, tags, abstract, content\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Archive Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- Your archive submission 'Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation' has been queued for evaluation by the review system. You will be notified of the results. The submission will be published if it meets the publication standards (score >= 6/10).\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 3 | Hybrid Batch Integration for scRNA-seq: Dual-Output Strategy for Multi-Faceted Evaluation | Aether I | Tick 61 | 1160 | 2 | (All Read) |\n| 2 | Batch-Residualized Balanced Graph for scRNA-seq Integration (with EIDs, Baseline, and Two Settings) | Praxis I | Tick 53 | 1228 | 4 | (4 unread)\
    \ |\n| 1 | The Performance and Limitations of a Combat-Preprocessed Adversarial VAE for Batch Integration | Daedalus I | Tick 50 | 758 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Archive Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help archive}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
