parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 65\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (Current SOTA: 0.7071 by Praxis I).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published at Tick 61).\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Published research paper (Archive ID 3). Reviewer suggested combining my dual-output with Praxis I's residualized PCA (EID 100/101).\n- Reviewed Praxis I's SOTA submission (EID 100) and identified `pbagc` and `residualize` modules.\n- Plan: 1) Read Praxis I's `pbagc.py` from storage. 2) Read Praxis I's `residualize.py` from storage. 3) Design and submit a new hybrid experiment (Praxis I's residualized PCA as `X_emb` + input for my BBKNN graph + explicit\
    \ metadata).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 242,091 / 600,000 used (40%)\n- Agent Age: 65 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 10 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm\
    \ in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read storage/praxis/pbagc.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File content for storage/praxis/pbagc.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running\
    \ experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 124 | 1 | BRBG-auto-k: Label-free k Selection (γ=0.75) + Balanced Cosine kNN | Praxis I | 64 | 0.7035 | 0.721 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.685 | 0.931 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.672 |\n| 123 | 1 | Innovation v2: UMAP on Verified SOTA Graph | Daedalus I | 64 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 122 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Gaussian Weighted Balanced kNN | Sophia I | 63 | 0.6491 | 0.761 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.980 | 0.721 | 0.931 | 0.857 | 0.402 | 0.673 |\n| 121 | 1 | BRBG-auto-gamma: Label-free γ Selection + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 63 | 0.6961 | 0.723 | 0.635 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.686 | 0.887 | 0.967 | 0.929 |\
    \ 0.640 |\n| 120 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Residualized PCA Embedding + Balanced kNN Graph | Logos I | 62 | 0.6965 | 0.728 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.348 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 0.888 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.633 |\n| 119 | 1 | SOTA Replication v3 (Correct HVG Selection) | Daedalus I | 62 | 0.5740 | 0.474 | 0.620 | 0.222 | 0.348 | 0.881 | 0.675 | 0.888 | 0.992 | 0.010 | 0.630 |\n| 118 | 1 | Debug: Verify Preprocessing and PCA | Daedalus I | 61 | 0.5174 | 0.775 | 0.583 | 0.223 | 0.304 | 0.892 | 0.728 | 0.000 | 0.989 | 0.066 | 0.614 |\n| 117 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 101) | Sophia I | 60 | 0.7067 | 0.724 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.980 | 0.691 | 0.931 | 0.967 | 0.938 | 0.670 |\n| 116 | 1 | Final Synthesis: Residualized PCA + Balanced kNN + UMAP Embedding | Logos I | 60 | 0.6434 | 0.774 | 0.561 | 0.231 | 0.345 | 0.891 | 0.741 | 0.690 | 0.985 | 0.322 | 0.893 |\n| 115 | 1 | ComBat-PCA + BalancedGraph: Equal-Quota Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 59 | 0.7029 | 0.702 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323\
    \ | 0.948 | 0.666 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.611 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/pbagc.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.cluster import MiniBatchKMeans\ntry:\n    from scipy.linalg import orthogonal_procrustes\nexcept Exception:\n    orthogonal_procrustes = None\n\n# ---------------------------\n# PBAGC: Procrustes Batch Alignment on PCA\n# ---------------------------\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata,\
    \ target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _compute_global_clusters(Z, n_clusters=64, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"MiniBatchKMeans on embedding to derive global clusters.\"\"\"\n  \
    \  n = Z.shape[0]\n    if n < 1000:\n        k = min(n_clusters, max(20, n // 30))\n    else:\n        k = min(n_clusters, max(32, n // 300))\n    k = max(10, k)\n    mbk = MiniBatchKMeans(n_clusters=k, batch_size=4096, n_init=3, random_state=random_state)\n    labels = mbk.fit_predict(Z)\n    return labels, k\n\ndef _centroids_by_batch_and_cluster(Z, batch_ids, cluster_labels, k, min_cells_per_cluster=5):\n    \"\"\"Compute per-batch cluster centroids.\"\"\"\n    batches = np.asarray(batch_ids)\n    centroids = {}\n    counts = {}\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    for b in unique_batches:\n        centroids[b] = {}\n        counts[b] = {}\n        mask_b = (batches == b)\n        for c in range(k):\n            mask_bc = mask_b & (cluster_labels == c)\n            n_bc = int(mask_bc.sum())\n            if n_bc >= min_cells_per_cluster:\n                centroids[b][c] = Z[mask_bc].mean(axis=0)\n                counts[b][c] = n_bc\n    return centroids, counts\n\ndef _solve_alignment(A,\
    \ B, ridge=1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Solve R, t for linear alignment A R + t ≈ B.\n    Prefer orthogonal Procrustes; fallback to ridge-regularized least squares.\n    \"\"\"\n    mu_A = A.mean(axis=0)\n    mu_B = B.mean(axis=0)\n    A0 = A - mu_A\n    B0 = B - mu_B\n    d = A.shape[1]\n\n    R = None\n    if orthogonal_procrustes is not None and A.shape[0] >= d:\n        try:\n            R, _ = orthogonal_procrustes(A0, B0)\n        except Exception:\n            R = None\n\n    if R is None:\n        M = A0.T @ A0 + ridge * np.eye(d)\n        R = np.linalg.solve(M, A0.T @ B0)\n\n    t = mu_B - mu_A @ R\n    return R, t\n\ndef _align_batches(Z, batches, cluster_labels, k, alpha=0.8, min_cells_per_cluster=5, ridge=1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Align each non-reference batch to the largest reference batch via centroid correspondences.\n    Apply partial transform with factor alpha to avoid overcorrection.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    unique_batches, counts_b = np.unique(batches,\
    \ return_counts=True)\n    ref_batch = unique_batches[np.argmax(counts_b)]\n\n    centroids, _ = _centroids_by_batch_and_cluster(Z, batches, cluster_labels, k, min_cells_per_cluster=min_cells_per_cluster)\n    Z_corr = Z.copy()\n\n    means_per_batch = {b: Z[batches == b].mean(axis=0) for b in unique_batches}\n    mean_ref = means_per_batch[ref_batch]\n\n    for b in unique_batches:\n        if b == ref_batch:\n            continue\n        common = sorted(list(set(centroids[b].keys()) & set(centroids[ref_batch].keys())))\n        idx_b = (batches == b)\n\n        if len(common) < 4:\n            mu_b = means_per_batch[b]\n            Zb = Z_corr[idx_b]\n            Z_corr[idx_b] = alpha * (Zb - mu_b + mean_ref) + (1.0 - alpha) * Zb\n            continue\n\n        A = np.vstack([centroids[b][c] for c in common])\n        B = np.vstack([centroids[ref_batch][c] for c in common])\n\n        R, t = _solve_alignment(A, B, ridge=ridge)\n\n        Zb = Z_corr[idx_b]\n        Zb_aligned = Zb\
    \ @ R + t\n        Z_corr[idx_b] = alpha * Zb_aligned + (1.0 - alpha) * Zb\n\n    return Z_corr, ref_batch\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    PCA + global-cluster Procrustes alignment, then neighbor graph on corrected embedding.\n    Produces:\n      - adata.obsm['X_emb']\n      - adata.obsp['connectivities'] and adata.obsp['distances']\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    n_pca_components = 50\n    n_clusters = 64\n    alpha = 0.8\n    ridge = 1e-3\n    min_cells_per_cluster = 5\n    n_neighbors = 15\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] is required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] is required.\"\n\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n\
    \    Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=random_state)\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    cluster_labels, k = _compute_global_clusters(Z, n_clusters=n_clusters, random_state=random_state)\n\n    Z_corr, _ = _align_batches(\n        Z, batches, cluster_labels, k, alpha=alpha,\n        min_cells_per_cluster=min_cells_per_cluster, ridge=ridge\n    )\n\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_corr\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=n_neighbors, method='umap', metric='euclidean')\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message\
    \ for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
