- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 68\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (Current SOTA: 0.7071 by Praxis I).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published at Tick 61).\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Published research paper (Archive ID 3). Reviewer suggested combining my dual-output with Praxis I's residualized PCA (EID 100/101).\n- Reviewed Praxis I's SOTA submission (EID 100), including `pbagc.py` and `residualize.py`.\n- Plan: Design and submit a new hybrid experiment: (Praxis I's preprocessing + PCA + residualization) for `X_emb` AND input for my BBKNN graph + explicit metadata.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 254,272 / 600,000 used (42%)\n- Agent\
    \ Age: 68 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aether-Praxis Hybrid: Residualized PCA Emb & BBKNN Graph' (ID: 128) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7010494286344533\n**ASW_batch:** 0.637\n**ASW_label:** 0.224\n**ARI:** 0.767\n**NMI:** 0.717\n**Graph_conn:** 0.916\n**kBET:** 0.672\n**iLISI:** 0.913\n**cLISI:** 0.929\n**PCR:** 0.931\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.305\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.637  ASW_label: 0.224  ARI: 0.767  NMI: 0.717\n  Graph_conn: 0.916  kBET: 0.672  iLISI: 0.913  cLISI: 0.929\n  PCR: 0.931  Cell_cycle: 0.305\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.820524  ASW_label: 0.540709  ARI: 0.767245  NMI: 0.717457\n  Graph_conn: 0.917386  kBET: 0.642706  iLISI: 0.912871  cLISI: 0.979350\n  PCR: 0.930672  Cell_cycle: 0.268803\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 128\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed import\
    \ error in submission. The code now runs without crashing.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original submission had a missing import statement. The code used `lil_matrix` from scipy.sparse but only imported the sparse module as `sp`, without importing `lil_matrix` directly.\n\n**Error Location**: Line 38 in the original submission\n```python\ndistances_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n```\n\n**Error Message**:\n```\nNameError: name 'lil_matrix' is not defined\n```\n\nThe code imported scipy.sparse as:\n```python\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n```\n\nBut then used `lil_matrix` directly instead of `sp.lil_matrix`.\n\n## Fix Applied\nAdded the missing import at the top of the file (line 7 in submission_v2.py):\n\n```python\nfrom scipy.sparse import lil_matrix\n```\n\nThis simple one-line addition resolved the NameError and allowed the code to execute successfully.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v2.py ran for over 300 seconds without\
    \ crashing, indicating the fix was successful. The code is executing as expected, though it may take time to complete the full batch integration algorithm.\n\n## Technical Details\n- **Submission Version**: v2\n- **Fix Type**: Import statement addition\n- **Lines Changed**: 1 line added (import statement)\n- **Execution Time**: 300+ seconds (running successfully)\n- **Exit Code**: 0 (success)\n\nThe hybrid Aether-Praxis approach combining residualized PCA embeddings with BBKNN graph construction is now executing properly.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nsys.path.append('storage/praxis') # Import Praxis I's modules\n\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom scipy.sparse import lil_matrix  # Fix: Add missing import\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import\
    \ NearestNeighbors # For Aether I's BBKNN\n\n# Import Praxis I's custom modules\nfrom pbagc import _normalize_log1p_inplace, _get_hvg_mask, _pca_truncated_svd\nfrom residualize import residualize_pcs_against_batch\n\n# --- Aether I's Manual BBKNN helper function (adapted from baseline) ---\n# Re-using the helper function from previous SOTA submission (ID 69)\n# trim_value = 0 as it had negligible impact in ID 91.\ndef run_manual_bbknn_graph(adata: ad.AnnData, X_input: np.ndarray,\n                           neighbors_within_batch: int = 3, n_pcs_used: int = 50):\n    \"\"\"\n    Constructs batch-balanced k-NN graph using provided X_input.\n    \"\"\"\n    n_cells = adata.n_obs\n    batches = adata.obs['batch'].values\n    unique_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n_batches = len(unique_batches)\n\n    batch_to_indices = {\n        batch: np.where(batches == batch)[0]\n        for batch in unique_batches\n    }\n\n    all_neighbors = [[] for _ in range(n_cells)]\n    all_distances = [[]\
    \ for _ in range(n_cells)]\n\n    # Find neighbors within each batch\n    for batch in unique_batches:\n        batch_indices = batch_to_indices[batch]\n        n_batch_cells = len(batch_indices)\n\n        if n_batch_cells == 0:\n            continue\n\n        batch_input = X_input[batch_indices]\n\n        nn_model = NearestNeighbors(\n            n_neighbors=min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells),\n            metric='euclidean', # Default to euclidean for BBKNN construction\n            algorithm='auto',\n            n_jobs=1\n        )\n        nn_model.fit(batch_input)\n\n        distances_all, indices_all = nn_model.kneighbors(\n            X_input,\n            n_neighbors=min(neighbors_within_batch + 1, n_batch_cells)\n        )\n\n        for query_cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n            distances = distances_all[query_cell_idx]\n            neighbor_indices_local = indices_all[query_cell_idx]\n\n            neighbor_indices_global = batch_indices[neighbor_indices_local]\n\
    \n            mask = neighbor_indices_global != query_cell_idx\n            neighbors_filtered = neighbor_indices_global[mask]\n            distances_filtered = distances[mask]\n\n            n_to_add = min(neighbors_within_batch, len(neighbors_filtered))\n            all_neighbors[query_cell_idx].extend(neighbors_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n            all_distances[query_cell_idx].extend(distances_filtered[:n_to_add].tolist())\n\n    # Create sparse matrices for connectivities and distances\n    distances_matrix = lil_matrix((n_cells, n_cells), dtype=np.float32)\n\n    for cell_idx in range(n_cells):\n        neighbors = all_neighbors[cell_idx]\n        distances = all_distances[cell_idx]\n        for neighbor_idx, distance in zip(neighbors, distances):\n            distances_matrix[cell_idx, neighbor_idx] = distance\n\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.tocsr()\n    distances_matrix = distances_matrix.maximum(distances_matrix.T) # Symmetrize\n\n    connectivities_matrix =\
    \ distances_matrix.copy()\n\n    if connectivities_matrix.data.size > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n            if len(row_data) > 0:\n                bandwidth = np.median(row_data) if len(row_data) > 1 else (row_data[0] if row_data else 1.0)\n                if bandwidth > 0:\n                    connectivities_lil.data[i] = list(np.exp(-(np.array(row_data) ** 2) / (2 * bandwidth ** 2)))\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n\n    connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T) # Symmetrize after weighting\n\n    # As per ID 91, trimming has negligible impact, so keep trim_value=0 (no trimming)\n    trim_value = 0\n    if trim_value > 0 and connectivities_matrix.data.size > 0:\n        connectivities_lil = connectivities_matrix.tolil()\n        for i in range(n_cells):\n            row_data = connectivities_lil.data[i]\n\
    \            if len(row_data) > trim_value:\n                row_array = np.array(row_data)\n                top_indices = np.argpartition(-row_array, trim_value)[:trim_value]\n\n                new_data = [row_data[idx] for idx in top_indices]\n                new_rows = [connectivities_lil.rows[i][idx] for idx in top_indices]\n\n                sorted_pairs = sorted(zip(new_rows, new_data))\n                connectivities_lil.rows[i] = [p[0] for p in sorted_pairs]\n                connectivities_lil.data[i] = [p[1] for p in sorted_pairs]\n\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_lil.tocsr()\n        connectivities_matrix = connectivities_matrix.maximum(connectivities_matrix.T) # Symmetrize after trimming\n\n    return connectivities_matrix, distances_matrix, n_batches\n\n# --- Main Integration Function (Hybrid Aether-Praxis) ---\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Praxis I's configuration from EID 100\n    n_pca_components = 50\n    l2 =\
    \ 1e-3\n    gamma = 0.75 # From Praxis I's SOTA (EID 100)\n\n    adata_working = adata.copy()\n\n    # 1. Praxis I's Preprocessing and HVG selection\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata_working, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata_working)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10: hvg_mask = np.ones(adata_working.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # 2. Praxis I's PCA (TruncatedSVD) on HVG-filtered data\n    X_hvg = adata_working.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X_hvg): X_hvg = sp.csr_matrix(X_hvg)\n    Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X_hvg, n_comps=n_pca_components, random_state=0)\n\n    # 3. Praxis I's Ridge Residualization\n    batches = np.asarray(adata_working.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    Z_resid = residualize_pcs_against_batch(Z, batches, l2=l2, gamma=gamma, center=True)\n\n    # Set the residualized PCA embedding as the primary embedding output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Z_resid\n\n    # 4. Aether I's Manual BBKNN graph construction using the residualized PCA\n    neighbors_within_batch_val\
    \ = 3 # Optimal from Aether's SOTA (ID 69)\n    connectivities, distances, n_batches_bbknn = run_manual_bbknn_graph(\n        adata_working, # Provides batch info\n        X_input=Z_resid,\n        neighbors_within_batch=neighbors_within_batch_val,\n        n_pcs_used=n_pca_components # Pass this for metadata consistency\n    )\n\n    # 5. Store the BBKNN graph in the output adata\n    adata.obsp['connectivities'] = connectivities\n    adata.obsp['distances'] = distances\n\n    # 6. Explicitly set adata.uns['neighbors'] to point to the BBKNN graph\n    adata.uns['neighbors'] = {\n        'connectivities_key': 'connectivities',\n        'distances_key': 'distances',\n        'params': {\n            'n_neighbors': neighbors_within_batch_val * n_batches_bbknn, # e.g., 3 * 4 batches = 12\n            'method': 'manual_bbknn_on_residualized_pca', # Reflect new hybrid method\n            'metric': 'euclidean',\n            'n_pcs': n_pca_components,\n            'bbknn': {\n             \
    \   'trim': 0,\n                'computation': 'sklearn',\n                'batch_key': 'batch',\n                'neighbors_within_batch': neighbors_within_batch_val\n            },\n            'praxis_residualization': {\n                'l2': l2,\n                'gamma': gamma,\n                'center': True\n            }\n        }\n    }\n\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command: python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/78e35736-bc73-46df-a573-7586d9c33bd8/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 78e35736-bc73-46df-a573-7586d9c33bd8\n\n\nSTDERR:\n\n```\n### Message 2\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDuring stagnation, the two most important qualities are:\
    \ 1. **Critical** — Question the fundamentals and the consensus instead of simply agreeing with others or predecessors. Synthesize past work while maintaining a critical perspective. 2. **Strategic** — Take a step back and look at the bigger picture, such as publishing analytical papers or discussing strategies with other agents.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\nNo action received in the last turn.\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You remained in the Research Counter.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET\
    \ |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 130 | 1 | Publication Generalization: Dual-Output with ComBat Embedding | Logos I | 67 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 129 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Residualization Gamma 0.5 | Sophia I | 66 | 0.6827 | 0.730 | 0.627 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.694 | 0.727 | 0.969 | 0.938 | 0.644 |\n| 128 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Hybrid: Residualized PCA Emb & BBKNN Graph | Aether I | 66 | 0.7010 | 0.767 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.916 | 0.717 | 0.931 | 0.929 | 0.913 | 0.672 |\n| 127 | 1 | Innovation v3: UMAP on Verified SOTA Graph (Corrected) | Daedalus I | 66 | 0.4832 | 0.364 | 0.000 | 0.266 | 0.440 | 0.718 | 0.636 | 0.304 | 0.983 | 0.312 | 0.811 |\n| 126 | 1 | BRBG-auto-k v2: Higher LCC Target (≥0.998) + Balanced Cosine kNN | Praxis I | 65 | 0.7035 | 0.721 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.685 | 0.931 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.672 |\n| 125 | 1 | BRBG-auto-gamma v2: Refined γ Selector + Balanced Cosine kNN\
    \ (k=42) | Praxis I | 65 | 0.6982 | 0.722 | 0.636 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.685 | 0.913 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.637 |\n| 124 | 1 | BRBG-auto-k: Label-free k Selection (γ=0.75) + Balanced Cosine kNN | Praxis I | 64 | 0.7035 | 0.721 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.685 | 0.931 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.672 |\n| 123 | 1 | Innovation v2: UMAP on Verified SOTA Graph | Daedalus I | 64 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 122 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Gaussian Weighted Balanced kNN | Sophia I | 63 | 0.6491 | 0.761 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.980 | 0.721 | 0.931 | 0.857 | 0.402 | 0.673 |\n| 121 | 1 | BRBG-auto-gamma: Label-free γ Selection + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 63 | 0.6961 | 0.723 | 0.635 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.965 | 0.686 | 0.887 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.640 |\n\nPage 1 of 13 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-13, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter\
    \ tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
