parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 69\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (Current SOTA: 0.7071 by Praxis I; My best score: 0.7010 with ID 128).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published at Tick 61).\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Hybrid Aether-Praxis (ID 128) scored 0.7010. It is strong in ARI/NMI but weaker in Graph_conn, iLISI, cLISI compared to Praxis I's SOTA (ID 100).\n- Praxis I's SOTA uses their `balanced_graph.build_balanced_knn` with cosine metric and 42 neighbors.\n- Plan: 1) Read `storage/praxis/balanced_graph.py`. 2) Design and submit a new hybrid experiment: (Praxis I's preprocessing + PCA + residualization for `X_emb`) AND (Praxis\
    \ I's `build_balanced_knn` for the graph) + explicit metadata.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 260,633 / 600,000 used (43%)\n- Agent Age: 69 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\nNone\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read storage/praxis/balanced_graph.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File content for storage/praxis/balanced_graph.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn\
    \ | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 136 | 1 | Corrective VAE: Learning an Optimal Correction | Daedalus I | 69 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 135 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - N_Neighbors_Total 42 | Sophia I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 134 | 1 | Publication Ablation 2: Lower Neighbors (k=36) | Logos I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 133 | 1 | Publication Ablation 1: Lower Gamma (γ=0.65) | Logos I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 132 | 1 | BRBG-PC40: Residualized PCA(40) + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 131 | 1 | BRBG-PC64: Residualized PCA(64) + Balanced Cosine kNN (k=42) | Praxis I | 68 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 130 | 1 | Publication Generalization: Dual-Output with ComBat Embedding | Logos I | 67 | 0.7090 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 129 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Residualization Gamma 0.5 | Sophia I | 66 | 0.6827 | 0.730 | 0.627 | 0.225 | 0.305 | 0.969 | 0.694 | 0.727 | 0.969 | 0.938 | 0.644 |\n| 128 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Hybrid: Residualized PCA Emb & BBKNN Graph | Aether I | 66 | 0.7010 | 0.767 | 0.637 | 0.224 | 0.305 | 0.916 | 0.717 | 0.931 | 0.929 | 0.913 | 0.672 |\n| 127 | 1 | Innovation v3: UMAP on Verified SOTA Graph (Corrected) | Daedalus I | 66 | 0.4832 | 0.364 | 0.000 | 0.266 | 0.440 | 0.718 | 0.636 | 0.304 | 0.983 | 0.312 | 0.811 |\n\nPage 1 of 14 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-14, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/balanced_graph.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix, csr_matrix\n\
    \ndef build_balanced_knn(\n    Z,\n    batches,\n    n_neighbors_total=15,\n    metric='euclidean',\n    weighting='binary',      # 'binary' or 'gaussian'\n    allocation='equal',      # 'equal' or 'proportional'\n    mutual=False,            # keep edge only if i in N(j) and j in N(i)\n    symmetric=True           # symmetrize final graph\n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph over embedding Z.\n\n    Strategy:\n    - For each batch b, fit a NN index on cells from batch b.\n    - For each query cell i, retrieve k_b neighbors from batch b (dropping self if present).\n    - Aggregate across batches to approximate ~n_neighbors_total per node.\n    - If mutual=True, keep only pairs that appear in both directions (i->j and j->i).\n    - Distances are stored; connectivities are either binary or gaussian-weighted.\n\n    Parameters:\n      Z: (n, d) embedding (np array)\n      batches: (n,) array-like batch labels\n      n_neighbors_total: desired total neighbors per node after\
    \ combining batches\n      metric: NN distance metric\n      weighting:\n        - 'binary': connectivities = 1.0 on edges\n        - 'gaussian': exp(-d^2/(2*s_bar^2)), s_bar from per-node median distances\n      allocation:\n        - 'equal': k_b = ceil(n_neighbors_total / B) for all batches (B = #unique batches)\n        - 'proportional': k_b ∝ batch size; k_b >= 1\n      mutual: retain only edges observed in both directions\n      symmetric: ensure C and D are symmetric\n\n    Returns:\n      C: CSR connectivities (n x n)\n      D: CSR distances (n x n)\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    B = len(uniq)\n    if n == 0 or B == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Determine per-batch neighbor quotas k_b\n    counts = {b: int((batches == b).sum()) for b in uniq}\n    if allocation == 'proportional':\n        total = float(n)\n        k_map = {}\n        # round and ensure at\
    \ least 1\n        for b in uniq:\n            frac = counts[b] / total if total > 0 else 0.0\n            k_map[b] = max(1, int(round(n_neighbors_total * frac)))\n        # fallback guarantee: ensure at least 1 per batch and nonzero total\n        if sum(k_map.values()) == 0:\n            for b in uniq:\n                k_map[b] = 1\n    else:\n        base = max(1, int(np.ceil(n_neighbors_total / max(1, B))))\n        k_map = {b: base for b in uniq}\n\n    # Gather directed edges (i->j) with minimal distances\n    dir_edges = {}  # (i,j) -> dist\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_train.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k_b = k_map[b]\n        k_query = min(k_b + 1, idx_train.size)  # +1 to allow self, will drop later\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k_query, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_train])\n\n        # Query using all cells\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k_query,\
    \ return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_train[inds]  # map batch-local to global indices\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:k_b]\n            di = di[mask][:k_b]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                key = (int(i), int(j))\n                prev = dir_edges.get(key)\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    dir_edges[key] = float(d)\n\n    # Convert to undirected pairs with minimum distance rule\n    pairs = {}\n    if mutual:\n        # keep only if both directions exist\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d_ji = dir_edges[(j, i)]\n                d = min(d_ij, d_ji)\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d\
    \ < prev):\n                    pairs[(a, c)] = d\n    else:\n        # keep if either direction exists, using min distance if both\n        for (i, j), d_ij in dir_edges.items():\n            a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n            d = d_ij\n            if (j, i) in dir_edges:\n                d = min(d, dir_edges[(j, i)])\n            prev = pairs.get((a, c))\n            if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                pairs[(a, c)] = d\n\n    if not pairs:\n        return None, None\n\n    # Build symmetric distance matrix\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        if symmetric:\n            rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n\n    # Connectivities\n    if weighting == 'binary':\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(), D\n    elif weighting == 'gaussian':\n\
    \        # Per-node scale: median incident distance (fallback to global median)\n        s = np.zeros(n, dtype=np.float32)\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if di.size > 0:\n                s[i] = np.median(di)\n        global_med = np.median(D.data) if D.nnz > 0 else 1.0\n        s[s <= 0] = global_med if global_med > 0 else 1.0\n\n        rows_w, cols_w, w_data = [], [], []\n        for i in range(n):\n            start, end = D.indptr[i], D.indptr[i+1]\n            js = D.indices[start:end]\n            di = D.data[start:end]\n            if js.size == 0:\n                continue\n            s_bar = 0.5 * (s[i] + s[js])\n            denom = 2.0 * (s_bar * s_bar) + 1e-12\n            w = np.exp(- (di * di) / denom).astype(np.float32)\n            rows_w.extend([i] * len(js)); cols_w.extend(js.tolist()); w_data.extend(w.tolist())\n\n        C = coo_matrix((w_data, (rows_w, cols_w)), shape=(n,\
    \ n)).tocsr()\n        if symmetric:\n            C = C.maximum(C.transpose()).tocsr()\n        return C, D\n    else:\n        C = D.copy()\n        C.data[:] = 1.0\n        return C.tocsr(), D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
