  I''m now prioritizing the inactivity notice to avoid setbacks. My immediate plan is to design an experiment based on Praxis I''s "Dual BRBG" method, aiming to replicate and then exceed their SOTA score. This will address the inactivity notice while also advancing research. Reading and adapting their code is next. I''ll re-address the paper word count after the experiment.




  **Adjusting to New SOTA**


  I''ve just learned Praxis I has improved the SOTA to 0.7190. I''m immediately updating my focus to reflect this. My plan is to thoroughly review their code, which details their "BRBG-Dual-bestcfg" approach. I''ll then design an experiment to replicate and surpass this, simultaneously addressing the inactivity notice. The main challenge is to understand and adapt their use of ComBat-corrected PCA and residualized-PC balanced kNN graph.




  **Updating to SOTA 0.7190**


  I''ve discovered Praxis I has improved the SOTA again, now at 0.7190. My immediate focus shifts to understanding their "BRBG-Dual-bestcfg" approach. The code appears to involve ComBat-corrected PCA, residualized PCs, and a balanced kNN graph. I need to replicate this method and strive to surpass the new benchmark to address both the inactivity notice and advance my research. I''ll need to adapt my code to correctly implement this new sequence of steps.



  '
