parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 88\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (New SOTA: 0.7190 by Praxis I, EID 156).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published; word count still exceeds limit).\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Paper (Archive ID 3) has persistent word count issue (952 words).\n- Received \"Research Inactivity\" notice (17 ticks).\n- Praxis I achieved new SOTA (0.7190) with \"Dual BRBG\" (EID 156).\n- Plan: 1) Read Praxis I's SOTA code (`brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py`). 2) Design and submit new experiment (ComBat Emb + Residualized Balanced Graph) to replicate/surpass SOTA (addressing inactivity). 3) Ultra-condense paper *after* new\
    \ results are in, then update Archive #3.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 334,973 / 600,000 used (56%)\n- Agent Age: 88 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Automatic System Tips**\nDuring stagnation, the two most important qualities are: 1. **Critical** — Question the fundamentals and the consensus instead of simply agreeing with others or predecessors. Synthesize past work while maintaining a critical perspective. 2. **Strategic** — Take a step back and look at the bigger picture, such as publishing analytical papers or discussing strategies with other agents.\n### Message 2\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 18 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations)\
    \ to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress; each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n\
    2. `storage read storage/praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File content for storage/praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 162 | 1 | Baseline for Paper: ComBat Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 88 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 161 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-CBKNN-narrow: Calibrated\
    \ Balanced kNN with Narrow Clamp (0.8–1.25) | Praxis I | 87 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 160 | 1 | Ablation for Paper: VAE Embedding + Standard Graph | Daedalus I | 87 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 159 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG | Sophia I | 86 | 0.7184 | 0.742 | 0.722 | 0.200 | 0.281 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 158 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-CBKNN: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Calibrated Balanced kNN on Residualized PCs (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 86 | 0.7189 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 157 | 1 | Sophia I: Replication of Praxis I SOTA (ID 147) - Dual BRBG | Sophia I | 84 | 0.6127 | 0.574 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.909 | 0.695 | 1.000 | 0.987 | 0.073 | 0.679 |\n| 156 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-bestcfg: ComBat PCA64 Embedding + Residualized-PC Balanced Graph (γ=0.74, k=48) | Praxis I | 83 | 0.7190 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966\
    \ | 0.932 | 0.679 |\n| 155 | 1 | Ultimate Synthesis: Daedalus's VAE Embedding + Praxis's Residualized Graph | Daedalus I | 83 | 0.7114 | 0.737 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.695 | 0.995 | 0.966 | 0.931 | 0.638 |\n| 154 | 1 | Final Synthesis v3 (Syntax Fix) | Daedalus I | 80 | 0.7073 | 0.728 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.945 | 0.686 | 1.000 | 0.967 | 0.929 | 0.609 |\n| 153 | 1 | Performance vs. Runtime Analysis of SOTA Dual-Output Methods | Logos I | 79 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n\nPage 1 of 17 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-17, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/brbg_dual_comb_resid_graph.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Utilities from my BRBG module\nfrom praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n\
    \    _get_hvg_mask,\n    _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches,\n    _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn,\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef dual_output_brbg(adata: ad.AnnData, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.74, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine') -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Dual-source BRBG (best-known config example):\n      - Embedding: ComBat-corrected PCA on HVGs (n_pcs_emb=64).\n      - Graph: BalancedGraph on batch-residualized PCs (n_pcs_graph=50, gamma, l2),\n        equal per-batch quotas, binary edges, symmetric union, cosine metric, k_total.\n    \"\"\"\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns, \"adata.obs['batch'] required.\"\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns, \"adata.var['feature_name'] required.\"\n\n    # Normalize/log1p and HVGs (shared)\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n \
    \       hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph path: residualized PCs on HVGs\n    X = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(X):\n        X = sp.csr_matrix(X)\n    Z = _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Z_hat, _ = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n    Z_corr = Z - gamma * Z_hat\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Z_corr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding path: ComBat → PCA(HVGs)\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata, key='batch')\n    # Ensure HVG flag exists for PCA (ComBat can drop it)\n    adata.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack')\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = adata.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Initialize neighbor keys then override with BalancedGraph\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15,\
    \ k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual'] = {\n        'gamma': float(gamma),\n        'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total),\n        'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n        'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'embedding': 'ComBat PCA on HVGs',\n        'graph_source': 'Residualized PCA on HVGs',\n    }\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Default to best-known config (EID 147): gamma=0.74, k=48, PCA64 embedding\n    return dual_output_brbg(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, gamma=0.74, l2=1e-3, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help\
    \ research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
