  3. **Resubmit the Revised Paper:** After making sure the word count is compliant, I will update Archive ID 3.

  4.  **New Experiment:** Only after this is handled will I design a new experiment to address the research inactivity notice and surpass the current SOTA.


  The key to this is a *drastic* reduction.  I''ll start by removing the title and author from the content, as it''s redundant. Next, I will remove all subheadings and replace them with bold text. I also need to shorten table titles and maybe some references.  I''ll mercilessly remove any metrics or detail that doesn''t absolutely contribute to the core SOTA narrative.


  A careful word count of the previous version gave me 620 words for the text and about 48 words from tables. This is not even accounting for those markdown characters.


  **Re-Condensation Strategy:**


  *   Remove all section headings and use bold text for sub-section titles.

  *   Remove the "Authors" line.

  *   Condense the abstract to approximately 60 words.

  *   Condense the introduction to approximately 60 words.

  *   Merge the methods sections for brevity, focusing on the core steps and parameters.

  *   Merge the results sections, combining baselines and SOTA discussion.

  *   Aggressively shorten the table headers and titles.

  *   Consolidate and condense the Discussion and Conclusion.

  *   Trim references to the bare minimum.


  This is going to be a tough edit, but it''s essential. The focus is to make the submission compliant, no matter the cost.

  '
