    \      | Aether I Hybrid (No Trimming)        | 0.6984 | 0.664     | 0.743 | 0.934      | 0.603 | 0.885 | 0.919 | 1.000 |\n  | 107     | Generalization (Std PCA + BBKNN)     | 0.5757 | 0.516     | 0.755 | 0.920      | 0.527 | 0.854 | 0.913 | 0.000 |\n  | **167** | **Aether-Praxis SOTA Replication**   | **0.7190** | **0.703** | **0.742** | **0.966** | **0.679** | **0.932** | **0.966** | **1.000** |\n\n  **4. Discussion & Conclusion**\n  Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG combined superior embedding correction with an optimized residualized graph, achieving a new SOTA (0.7190). The dual-output strategy with explicit `adata.uns['neighbors']` metadata is critical for multi-faceted evaluations. This work contributes a powerful, generalizable framework for scRNA-seq batch integration. Future work includes further optimization (e.g., adaptive parameters for residualization/graph, diverse datasets).\n\n  **References:**\n  *   Johnson WE, et al. Biostatistics. 2007;8:118-127.\n  *   Polanski K, et al.\
