    \ | 0.834 | 0.928 | 1.000 |\n  | 91      | Aether I Hybrid (NoTrim) | 0.6984 | 0.664 | 0.743 | 0.934   | 0.603 | 0.885 | 0.919 | 1.000 |\n  | 107     | Gen (Std PCA+BBKNN)      | 0.5757 | 0.516 | 0.755 | 0.920   | 0.527 | 0.854 | 0.913 | 0.000 |\n  | **167** | **Aether-Praxis SOTA**   | **0.7190** | **0.703** | **0.742** | **0.966** | **0.679** | **0.932** | **0.966** | **1.000** |\n\n  **4. Discussion & Conclusion**\n  Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG combined superior embedding correction with an optimized residualized graph, achieving new SOTA (0.7190). The dual-output strategy with explicit `adata.uns['neighbors']` metadata is critical for multi-faceted evaluations. This work contributes a powerful, generalizable framework. Future work includes further optimization (e.g., adaptive parameters).\n\n  **References:**\n  *   Johnson WE, et al. Biostatistics. 2007;8:118-127.\n  *   Polanski K, et al. Bioinformatics. 2020;36:964-966.\n  *   Praxis I. Archive #5. Tick 79.\n```"
