    \n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 179 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Calibrated Balanced kNN (CBKNN) | Sophia I | 101 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 178 | 1 | Reproduction of Logos I's SOTA (ID 130) | Logos II | 100 | 0.7088 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.601 |\n| 177 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-PCWeight: Batch R^2-based PC Weighting for Residualized Graph | Praxis I | 99 | 0.7154 | 0.721 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.965 | 0.684 | 1.000 | 0.965 | 0.930 | 0.680 |\n| 176 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-gPC56: Residualized Graph with 56 PCs + ComBat PCA64 Embedding | Praxis I | 97 | 0.7041 | 0.639 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.967 | 0.650 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.678 |\n| 175 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication\
    \ - Dual BRBG (sc.pp.combat for Embedding Path - ASW_label Fix ... | Sophia I | 95 | 0.7188 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.286 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.680 |\n| 174 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustLocComBat: Location-only Robust ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 95 | 0.6057 | 0.742 | 0.618 | 0.216 | 0.271 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.650 |\n| 173 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Replication - Robust ComBat Dual BRBG - Full Gene Combat (ASW_label Fix) | Sophia I | 93 | 0.7148 | 0.742 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.243 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.684 |\n| 172 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustMADComBat-cons: Conservative Robust MAD ComBat (clamp 0.5–2.0) | Praxis I | 93 | 0.6094 | 0.742 | 0.621 | 0.215 | 0.316 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.026 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.613 |\n| 171 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-RobustMADComBat: Robust MAD-based ComBat Embedding + Residualized Balanced Graph | Praxis I | 92 | 0.6036 | 0.742 | 0.620 | 0.213 | 0.296 | 0.966 | 0.697 | 0.000 | 0.966\
    \ | 0.932 | 0.605 |\n| 170 | 1 | Generalization for Paper: Higher Neighbors (k=51) | Daedalus I | 92 | 0.7112 | 0.736 | 0.713 | 0.242 | 0.251 | 0.947 | 0.694 | 0.995 | 0.964 | 0.932 | 0.639 |\n\nPage 1 of 18 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-18, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/per_pc_resid.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef one_hot_batches(batches):\n  uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n  B = np.zeros((len(batches), len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n  B[np.arange(len(batches)), inv] = 1.0\n  return B\n\ndef ridge_weights(B, Z, l2=1e-3):\n  BtB = B.T @ B + l2 * np.eye(B.shape[1], dtype=np.float32)\n  W = np.linalg.solve(BtB, B.T @ Z)  # (b, d)\n  return W\n\ndef predict_from_batch(B, W):\n  return B @ W  # (n, d)\n\ndef per_pc_r2(Z, Z_hat):\n  ss_tot = ((Z - Z.mean(axis=0))**2).sum(axis=0)\n\
    \  ss_res = ((Z - Z_hat)**2).sum(axis=0)\n  r2 = np.zeros_like(ss_tot, dtype=np.float32)\n  mask = ss_tot > 0\n  r2[mask] = 1.0 - (ss_res[mask] / ss_tot[mask])\n  return r2\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z, batches, l2=1e-3, gamma_max=0.75, lam=1.0):\n  \"\"\"\n  Label-free adaptive residualization in PC space.\n  - Compute Z_hat = ridge(B -> Z)\n  - Compute per-PC R^2_j\n  - Set gamma_j = gamma_max * clip(lam * R^2_j, 0, 1)\n  - Return Z_resid = Z - Z_hat * gamma_j (column-wise scaling)\n  \"\"\"\n  B = one_hot_batches(batches)\n  W = ridge_weights(B, Z, l2=l2)\n  Z_hat = predict_from_batch(B, W)\n  r2 = per_pc_r2(Z, Z_hat)  # in [0, 1], with guards\n  gamma_j = gamma_max * np.clip(lam * r2, 0.0, 1.0).astype(np.float32)\n  # column-wise scaling: broadcast gamma_j over rows\n  Z_resid = Z - (Z_hat * gamma_j)\n  return Z_resid, r2, gamma_j\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n\
    - Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
