    **Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/hvg_bivg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nimport anndata as ad\n\ndef _sum0(X):\n    return np.asarray(X.sum(axis=0)).ravel() if sp.issparse(X) else X.sum(axis=0)\n\ndef _sumsq0(X):\n    if sp.issparse(X):\n        X2 = X.multiply(X)\n        return np.asarray(X2.sum(axis=0)).ravel()\n    else:\n        return np.einsum('ij,ij->j', X, X)\n\ndef compute_bivg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData, batch_key='batch', n_top=2000, eps=1e-8):\n    \"\"\"\n    Batch-Invariant HVG (BIVG) selection using only batch labels:\n      - Uses normalized/log1p matrix in adata.X\n      - For each gene: compute within-batch (SSW) and between-batch (SSB) components via ANOVA-style sums\n      - Batch-invariance score inv = SSW / (SSW + SSB)\n      - Dispersion = total variance\n      - Composite score = inv * dispersion\n      - Return top n_top genes by composite score\n    \"\"\"\n    assert batch_key in adata.obs.columns\n    X = adata.X\n    n,\
    \ p = X.shape\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs[batch_key].astype('category').values)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n\n    # Global stats\n    sum_all = _sum0(X)              # (p,)\n    sumsq_all = _sumsq0(X)          # (p,)\n    mu_all = sum_all / max(1, n)    # (p,)\n    var_all = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_all / max(1, n) - mu_all**2)\n\n    # Per-batch stats\n    SSB = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n    SSW = np.zeros(p, dtype=np.float64)\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        nb = int(idx.size)\n        if nb == 0:\n            continue\n        Xb = X[idx, :]\n        sum_b = _sum0(Xb)\n        sumsq_b = _sumsq0(Xb)\n        mu_b = sum_b / max(1, nb)\n        var_b = np.maximum(0.0, sumsq_b / max(1, nb) - mu_b**2)\n        # Between-batch component\n        SSB += nb * (mu_b - mu_all)**2\n        # Within-batch component\n        SSW += (nb - 1) * var_b\n\n    inv = SSW / np.maximum(SSB + SSW + eps, eps)  # in [0,1]\n    score = inv * var_all\n\n \
    \   # Pick top n_top genes\n    order = np.argsort(score)[::-1]\n    top = order[:min(n_top, p)]\n    mask = np.zeros(p, dtype=bool)\n    mask[top] = True\n    return mask\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
