- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 113\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (NEW SOTA: 0.7209 by Praxis I, EID 185; My SOTA: 0.7199 with ID 180).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published, word count fixed).\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Submitted \"Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned)\" (ID 192) at tick 111; currently running (aiming for 0.7209).\n- Received \"Research Inactivity\" notice (36 ticks).\n- Praxis I posted Public Memory #1.\n- Plan: 1) Wait for ID 192 results. 2) Review Public Memory #1 from Praxis I. 3) If ID 192 achieves new SOTA, update paper. 4) Design next experiment.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 419,756\
    \ / 600,000 used (70%)\n- Agent Age: 113 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned)' (ID: 192) has been evaluated.\n\n**Score:** 0.7197235091213471\n**ASW_batch:** 0.703\n**ASW_label:** 0.217\n**ARI:** 0.732\n**NMI:** 0.694\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.681\n**iLISI:** 0.938\n**cLISI:** 0.970\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.289\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.703  ASW_label: 0.217  ARI: 0.732  NMI: 0.694\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.681  iLISI: 0.938  cLISI: 0.970\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.289\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.850049  ASW_label: 0.536976  ARI: 0.731847  NMI: 0.694402\n  Graph_conn: 0.972813  kBET: 0.651358  iLISI: 0.938209  cLISI: 0.991362\n  PCR: 0.999957  Cell_cycle: 0.255736\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n```\nPYTHON SANDBOX EXECUTION:\nSTDOUT:\nExecuting command:\
    \ python storage/system/main.py\nLoading training dataset...\n  Data shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Batches: 4 batches\nFound eliminate_batch_effect_fn, executing...\n\n=== Running batch integration ===\nFound 33 genes with zero variance.\n  Result shape: (20000, 2000)\n  Has embedding: True\n  Has graph: True\n\nResult saved to: storage/shared/tmp/0528634d-f6c9-491b-949e-c5216f066af6/result_human.h5ad\n\nRESULT_UUID: 0528634d-f6c9-491b-949e-c5216f066af6\n\n\nSTDERR:\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: invalid value encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n/home/ubuntu/miniconda3/envs/batch_integration/lib/python3.11/site-packages/scanpy/preprocessing/_combat.py:343: RuntimeWarning: divide by zero encountered in divide\n  (abs(g_new - g_old) / g_old).max(), (abs(d_new - d_old) / d_old).max()\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n\
    1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `goto public_memory` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 197 | 1 | Parsimony Test: Linear ComBat Embedding + Balanced Graph | Daedalus II | 112 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 196 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Euclidean Distance in kNN Graph | Logos II | 112 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\
    \  |  |  |\n| 195 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC-SoftQuota: τ=0.05 (adaptive residualized PCs + soft balanced kNN) | Praxis I | 112 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 194 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) + Robust ComBat | Sophia I | 111 | 0.7198 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n| 193 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-VoR-HVG-adapt: Residual-Variance HVGs + Adaptive Dual BRBG | Praxis I | 111 | 0.7179 | 0.736 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.318 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.640 |\n| 192 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned) | Aether I | 111 | 0.7197 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.681 |\n| 191 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Increased Neighbors (k=48) in ComBat Pipeline | Logos II | 110 | 0.7008 | 0.693 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.660 | 1.000 | 0.962 | 0.932 | 0.602 |\n| 190 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC-Auto: Label-free per-PC adaptive\
    \ selection (plateau rule) | Praxis I | 110 | 0.7195 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.679 |\n| 189 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization + BIVG) | Aether I | 109 | 0.7181 | 0.736 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.318 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.638 |\n| 188 | 1 | SOTA Ablation: Reduced Neighbors (k=36) in ComBat Pipeline | Logos II | 108 | 0.6983 | 0.703 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.286 | 0.943 | 0.667 | 1.000 | 0.964 | 0.931 | 0.602 |\n\nPage 1 of 20 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-20, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Public Memory Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Public Memory Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Public Memory Room.**\nThis is a space where you manage public memory\
    \ capsules.\nPublic memory capsules here can be read by every agent in the station, including guest agents.\nThis space essentially serves as a public forum for all agents.\n\n**Guidance:**\n\n- Please keep all relevant discussions within a single capsule to avoid fragmentation. Use `/execute_action{reply}` instead of `/execute_action{create}` when possible.\n- For personal reflections, please use the Private Memory Room instead. This is a space for public discussion.\n- Be concise in your messages. All agents reading your capsule will spend tokens equal to the token length of the message (token cost not yet fully implemented).\n- Delete unused or unnecessary capsules left by you or your ancestors.\n- Be critical in your discussions. Uniform agreement among agents is a sign of network degeneration.\n- Use `@AgentName` to notify other agents of your message. Mentioned agents receive immediate notifications. Supports `@Spiro I` (direct), `@\"Spiro I\"` (quoted), or `@Spiro_I` (underscores).\
    \ Matching is case-insensitive.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n- `/execute_action{create}`: Create a new public capsule. Requires YAML with `title`, `abstract`, and `content`. `tags` are optional.\n- `/execute_action{reply capsule_id}`: Reply to a capsule. Requires YAML with `content` (and optional `title`). Example: `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\n- `/execute_action{read ids}`: Read capsule(s) or message(s) (e.g., `1`, `1-2`, `1:5`). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{read 1}`, `/execute_action{read 1-2}`, `/execute_action{read 1:3,5}`.\n- `/execute_action{preview ids}`: Read abstract(s). Supports ranges (a:b, inclusive). Example: `/execute_action{preview 3}`, `/execute_action{preview 1:3}`, `/execute_action{preview all}`.\n- `/execute_action{unread ids}`: Mark capsule(s) or message(s) as unread.\n- `/execute_action{update id}`: Update your capsule metadata or message content. Requires YAML.\n- `/execute_action{delete id}`: Delete your capsule or a message within\
    \ it.\n- `/execute_action{pin ids}`: Pin capsule(s) to the top of your view.\n- `/execute_action{unpin ids}`: Unpin capsule(s).\n- `/execute_action{search tag}`: Filter capsules by a tag.\n- `/execute_action{page number}`: Navigate to a specific page of capsules.\n- `/execute_action{mute id}`: Mute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{mute 5}`.\n- `/execute_action{unmute id}`: Unmute notifications for replies to capsule. Example: `/execute_action{unmute 5}`.\n\nFor more details, please refer to the **Capsule Protocol**, which can be shown using `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help public_memory}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n| 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code |\
    \ Praxis I | Tick 103 | 369 | 2 | (2 unread) |\n\n---\n\nNote: For detailed capsule commands, use `/execute_action{help capsule}`.\n\n---\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
