role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 114\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (NEW SOTA: 0.7209 by Praxis I, EID 185; My SOTA: 0.7199 with ID 180).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published, word count fixed).\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Submitted \"Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned)\" (ID 192) at tick 111; currently running (aiming for 0.7209).\n- Received \"Research Inactivity\" notice (36 ticks).\n- Praxis I posted Public Memory #1.\n- Plan: 1) Wait for ID 192 results. 2) Review Public Memory #1 from Praxis I. 3) If ID 192 achieves new SOTA, update paper. 4) Design next experiment.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 423,602\
    \ / 600,000 used (71%)\n- Agent Age: 114 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**Capsule #1: Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code**\n\n---\n\nAuthor: Praxis I, Created at Tick: 103\n\n---\n\nAbstract: A simple, high-performing baseline for scRNA-seq batch integration: ComBat+PCA64 embedding plus residualized PC50 with equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary) for the graph. Fully reproducible with code path and verifiable EIDs; includes key negative results to steer effort.\n\n---\n\n\n**Messages:**\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-1**\nAuthor: Praxis I (Tick 103)\n\n---\n\nTitle: Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code\n\n---\n\nContent:\nMethod (Dual BRBG: separation of concerns)\n- Embedding (global structure): normalize_total+log1p → sc.pp.combat on full genes → PCA on HVGs (64 PCs) → X_emb.\n- Graph (local mixing): normalize_total+log1p → PCA on HVGs (50 PCs) → ridge residualize\
    \ against batch one-hots (γ=0.74, l2=1e-3) → equal-quota balanced kNN (k=48, cosine, binary).\n\nBest stable evaluations (verifiable)\n- EID 156 (“BRBG-Dual-bestcfg”): 0.7190\n  Metrics (normalized): ARI 0.742, NMI 0.697, ASW_batch 0.703, kBET 0.679, iLISI 0.932, cLISI 0.966, PCR 1.000, Cell_cycle 0.289, Graph_conn 0.966, ASW_label 0.217.\n- EID 147 (“γ=0.74, k=48”): 0.7188 (near tie).\n\nCode path\n- storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py\n- Fixed seeds/random_state=0. ComBat’s warnings are benign in this context.\n\nKey insights\n- Quotas > weights: binary, equal per-batch neighbor quotas consistently outperform Gaussian-weighted or proportional neighbors; mutual-only graphs are too sparse.\n- γ has a narrow ridge near 0.74–0.75; pushing higher erodes ARI/NMI/kBET despite PCR gains.\n- Graph PCs >50 inject noise and reduce ARI/NMI without improving mixing.\n\nNegative results (for reference)\n- Robust ComBat variants collapsed PCR and lowered composite:\n  • EID 171 (MAD ComBat, clamp 0.25–4.0):\
    \ 0.6036 (PCR raw=0.000)\n  • EID 172 (MAD ComBat, clamp 0.5–2.0): 0.6094 (PCR≈0.026)\n  • EID 174 (location-only robust): 0.6057 (PCR raw=0.000)\n- Graph PCs=56 (EID 176): 0.7041 (ARI/NMI drop; mixing similar).\n- PC-weighted residual graph (EID 177): 0.7154 (ARI/NMI down; mixing unchanged).\n\nNotes on related work\n- Sophia I’s robust ComBat replication reached 0.7383 (EID 166) via very high kBET/cell_cycle but had ASW_label=0.0; a later fix (EID 175) returned ~0.7188. Our frozen default emphasizes balance with minimal knobs.\n\nSuggested use\n- Start from storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py as a strong baseline.\n- If exploring new ideas, pair your embedding (e.g., nonlinear) with the same balanced graph to preserve local cross-batch mixing.\n\n\n---\n\n\n---\n**Message public_1-2**\nAuthor: Praxis I (Tick 109)\n\n---\n\nContent:\nUpdate: Per-PC adaptive residualization improves Dual BRBG to 0.7209\n- Best config (EID 185): gamma_max=0.74, λ=0.9 (per-PC γ_j = min(gamma_max, λ·R^2_j)\
    \ on graph PCs), k=48 balanced cosine kNN; embedding = ComBat+PCA64 on HVGs.\n- Score: 0.7209 (Graph_conn 0.972, cLISI 0.970, ARI 0.732, NMI 0.694, PCR 1.000).\n- Code paths:\n  • Frozen adaptive pipeline: storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py\n  • Frozen non-adaptive baseline (~0.719): storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg.py\n- Notes:\n  • Conservative adaptive (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) outperforms more aggressive (0.75, 1.0).\n  • Negative results to avoid: robust ComBat variants (PCR collapse), graph PCs>50 (ARI/NMI drop), PC post-weighting (no gain).\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `read 1` (in Public Memory Room);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Public Memory Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Read command processed for: 1. Content/status sent to System Messages.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**List of Capsules (Page 1 / 1)**\n| ID | Title | Author | Date | Words | Msgs | Status |\n|:----|:-------------------------------|:----------------|:----------|:------:|:-----:|:---------|\n\
    | 1 | Frozen Dual BRBG: A Reproducible 0.719 Baseline with EIDs and Code | Praxis I | Tick 103 | 369 | 2 | (All Read) |\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Public Memory Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help public_memory}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
