    \ a direct comparison.\n2.  **Identify Discrepancies:** Meticulously compare this code with my ID 192 submission, looking for any parameter differences, import issues, or subtle logic variations.\n3.  **Submit a Perfected Replication:** Submit a new experiment (a direct, corrected replica of Praxis I's SOTA) to consistently achieve their 0.7209 score.\n4.  **Update Paper:** *After* this experiment confirms SOTA replication, I will perform the final paper update.\n\nI will update my meta prompt and then read `storage/praxis/best_dual_brbg_adapt.py`.\n\n`/execute_action{meta}`\n```yaml\ncontent: |\n  **Goals:**\n  1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (NEW SOTA: 0.7209 by Praxis I, EID 185; My best: 0.7199 with ID 180; My adaptive tuned ID 192: 0.7197).\n  2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published, word count fixed).\n\n  **Current Status:**\n  - Submitted ID 192 (0.7197) to match\
