    \ integrating this concept into my Dual BRBG adaptive framework (addressing inactivity with a novel approach).\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 450,391 / 600,000 used (75%)\n- Agent Age: 122 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n**PRE-WARNING:** You have used 450,391 tokens, which is over 75% of your current budget limit of 600,000.\n\nYou are advised to go to the Token Management Room to prune outdated data in order to reduce token usage. Please issue `/execute_action{help token_management}` for strategies on how to use the Token Management Room effectively.\n\nIf you decide not to prune token usage and plan to leave the station, you should leave an important message for your future descendant in the Private Memory Capsule Room. You can still continue normal operations, as it is generally safe to remain at the station when you have more than 10,000 tokens remaining.\n\nYou should carefully consider whether to prune previous responses or to leave the station.\
    \ Spawning a new agent takes time and often disrupts existing projects. Your descendant is not you—they only inherit a portion of your memory. However, they may offer a fresh perspective to the station.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_fused.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File content for storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_fused.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n**Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label |\
    \ Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 208 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-FusedGeom: Two-View Equal-Quota Graph (k=48, geomean fusion) | Praxis I | 121 | running |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 207 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-Fused: Two-View Equal-Quota Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 120 | 0.7177 | 0.735 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.318 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.935 | 0.637 |\n| 206 | 1 | Distilled VAE Embedding + Balanced Graph | Daedalus II | 119 | 0.7179 | 0.747 | 0.604 | 0.235 | 0.356 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.691 |\n| 205 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Final Import Fix) | Aether I | 119 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 204 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-MinQuota: Min-2-per-batch + Global Fill (k=48) | Praxis I | 118 | 0.6422 | 0.778 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.315 | 0.971 | 0.732 | 1.000 | 0.980 | 0.100 | 0.637 |\n| 203 | 1\
    \ | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-PCA72: ComBat PCA72 + Adaptive Residualized Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 118 | 0.7123 | 0.736 | 0.706 | 0.215 | 0.279 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.612 |\n| 202 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Precise) | Aether I | 118 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 201 | 1 | Sophia I: Aether I SOTA Replication - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.75, λ=1.0) + Robust ComBa... | Sophia I | 117 | 0.7198 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.683 |\n| 200 | 1 | Novel Method: Stabilized ComBat Implementation | Logos II | 114 | 0.7090 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n| 199 | 1 | Sophia I: Praxis I SOTA Optimization - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) + Robust ComB... | Sophia I | 114 | 0.7190 | 0.729 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.970 | 0.692 | 1.000 | 0.968 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages\
    \ 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_fused.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\nfrom scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn_fused(Z_corr, Z_emb, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine', extra=4):\n    \"\"\"\n    Equal per-batch quotas using fused per-batch distances:\n    For each batch b and cell i, candidate neighbors are the union of top (per_batch+extra) neighbors\n    from Z_corr and Z_emb within batch b. Fused distance d_fused = min(d_corr, d_emb)\
    \ on the candidate set.\n    Build an undirected graph from per-batch selections; binary connectivities; distances = fused.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z_corr = np.asarray(Z_corr, dtype=np.float32)\n    Z_emb = np.asarray(Z_emb, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z_corr.shape[0]\n    per_batch = int(np.ceil(k_total / max(1, uniq.shape[0])))\n\n    # Pre-fit per-batch NN indices for both views\n    nn_corr = {}\n    nn_emb = {}\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx.size == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(per_batch + extra + 1, idx.size)\n        nnc = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nne = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nnc.fit(Z_corr[idx])\n        nne.fit(Z_emb[idx])\n        nn_corr[b] = (idx, nnc)\n        nn_emb[b] = (idx, nne)\n\n    pairs_min_dist = {}\n\n    for b in uniq:\n        idx_train, nnc = nn_corr[b]\n\
    \        _, nne = nn_emb[b]\n        k = min(per_batch + extra + 1, idx_train.size)\n\n        # Corr-space neighbors\n        d_c, ind_c = nnc.kneighbors(Z_corr, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        g_c = idx_train[ind_c]\n\n        # Emb-space neighbors\n        d_e, ind_e = nne.kneighbors(Z_emb, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        g_e = idx_train[ind_e]\n\n        for i in range(n):\n            # Collect candidate set from both views\n            cand = {}\n            # Corr view\n            for gj, dj in zip(g_c[i], d_c[i]):\n                if gj == i: continue\n                prev_c, prev_e = cand.get(gj, (np.inf, np.inf))\n                cand[gj] = (min(prev_c, float(dj)), prev_e)\n            # Emb view\n            for gj, dj in zip(g_e[i], d_e[i]):\n                if gj == i: continue\n                prev_c, prev_e = cand.get(gj, (np.inf, np.inf))\n                cand[gj] = (prev_c, min(prev_e, float(dj)))\n            # Compute fused distances and\
    \ select top per_batch\n            items = []\n            for gj, (dc, de) in cand.items():\n                df = min(dc, de)\n                items.append((gj, df))\n            items.sort(key=lambda x: x[1])\n            for gj, df in items[:per_batch]:\n                a, c = (i, gj) if i < gj else (gj, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (df < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = df\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows += [i, j]; cols += [j, i]; dist_data += [d, d]\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy(); C.data[:] = 1.0\n    return C, D\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Dual BRBG with fused two-view balanced graph:\n      - Graph view: residualized PCs (adaptive per-PC: gamma_j=min(0.74, 0.9*R^2_j)),\
    \ PCs=50.\n      - Embedding view: ComBat on normalized/log1p + PCA64 (HVGs).\n      - Build equal-quota balanced kNN per batch using fused per-batch distances d_fused = min(d_corr, d_emb).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Config\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    extra = 4\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph view (Z_corr)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\
    \    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n\n    # Embedding view (Z_emb)\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Build fused balanced graph\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_fused(Zcorr, Zemb, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric, extra=extra)\n\n    # Output embedding and graph\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_fused']\
    \ = {\n        'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'fusion': 'min(d_corr, d_emb)', 'extra': int(extra)\n    }\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
