    \ | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 204 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-MinQuota: Min-2-per-batch + Global Fill (k=48) | Praxis I | 118 | 0.6422 | 0.778 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.315 | 0.971 | 0.732 | 1.000 | 0.980 | 0.100 | 0.637 |\n| 203 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-PCA72: ComBat PCA72 + Adaptive Residualized Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 118 | 0.7123 | 0.736 | 0.706 | 0.215 | 0.279 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.612 |\n| 202 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Precise) | Aether I | 118 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 201 | 1 | Sophia I: Aether I SOTA Replication - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.75, λ=1.0) + Robust ComBa... | Sophia I | 117 | 0.7198 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.683 |\n| 200 | 1 | Novel Method: Stabilized ComBat Implementation | Logos II | 114 | 0.7090 | 0.748 | 0.664 | 0.223 | 0.323 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.602 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page\
    \ N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/auto_gamma_brbg.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\nfrom sklearn.decomposition import TruncatedSVD\nfrom sklearn.neighbors import NearestNeighbors\n\n# ---------------------------\n# Shared utilities for BRBG\n# ---------------------------\n\ndef _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata: ad.AnnData, target_sum: float = 1e4):\n    \"\"\"Normalize raw counts and log1p in-place.\"\"\"\n    if 'counts' in adata.layers:\n        adata.X = adata.layers['counts'].copy()\n    sc.pp.normalize_total(adata, target_sum=target_sum, inplace=True)\n    sc.pp.log1p(adata)\n\ndef _get_hvg_mask(adata: ad.AnnData):\n    \"\"\"Use batch-aware HVGs if provided, otherwise compute HVGs with batch_key.\"\"\"\n    if 'batch_hvg' in\
    \ adata.var.columns:\n        mask = np.asarray(adata.var['batch_hvg'].values, dtype=bool)\n        if mask.sum() > 0:\n            return mask\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    return np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\ndef _pca_truncated_svd(X, n_comps=50, random_state=0):\n    \"\"\"Sparse-aware PCA via TruncatedSVD.\"\"\"\n    n_comps = max(2, min(n_comps, X.shape[1]-1 if X.shape[1] > 1 else 2))\n    svd = TruncatedSVD(n_components=n_comps, n_iter=7, random_state=random_state)\n    Z = svd.fit_transform(X)\n    return Z\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n    B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n    B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n    return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n    \"\"\"\n    Ridge\
    \ fit batch one-hot B to predict PCs Z. Returns Z_hat (n x d) and W (b x d).\n    \"\"\"\n    BtB = B.T @ B\n    W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n    Z_hat = B @ W\n    return Z_hat, W\n\ndef _build_balanced_knn(Z: np.ndarray, batches, k_total=48, metric='cosine'):\n    \"\"\"\n    Build a batch-balanced kNN graph:\n      - Equal per-batch quotas (distributes remainder across batches in order)\n      - Binary connectivities (1.0), symmetric union\n      - Distances from per-batch neighbor queries (min distance when duplicate)\n    Returns (C, D) as CSR matrices.\n    \"\"\"\n    Z = np.asarray(Z, dtype=np.float32)\n    batches = np.asarray(batches)\n    uniq_batches = np.unique(batches)\n    n = Z.shape[0]\n    nb = len(uniq_batches)\n    if nb == 0 or n == 0:\n        return None, None\n\n    base = k_total // nb\n    rem = k_total - base * nb\n    quotas = {b: base + (1 if i < rem else 0) for i, b in enumerate(uniq_batches)}\n\n    pairs_min_dist\
    \ = {}\n    for b in uniq_batches:\n        idx_b = np.where(batches == b)[0]\n        if idx_b.size == 0 or quotas[b] == 0:\n            continue\n        k = min(quotas[b] + 1, idx_b.size)  # +1 to allow self (to be dropped)\n        nn = NearestNeighbors(n_neighbors=k, metric=metric, algorithm='auto')\n        nn.fit(Z[idx_b])\n        dists, inds = nn.kneighbors(Z, n_neighbors=k, return_distance=True)\n        neigh_global = idx_b[inds]\n        for i in range(n):\n            g = neigh_global[i]\n            di = dists[i]\n            mask = g != i\n            g = g[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            di = di[mask][:quotas[b]]\n            for j, d in zip(g, di):\n                if i == j:\n                    continue\n                a, c = (i, j) if i < j else (j, i)\n                prev = pairs_min_dist.get((a, c))\n                if (prev is None) or (d < prev):\n                    pairs_min_dist[(a, c)] = float(d)\n\n    if not pairs_min_dist:\n        return None, None\n\n\
    \    rows, cols, dist_data = [], [], []\n    for (i, j), d in pairs_min_dist.items():\n        rows.append(i); cols.append(j); dist_data.append(d)\n        rows.append(j); cols.append(i); dist_data.append(d)\n\n    from scipy.sparse import coo_matrix\n    D = coo_matrix((dist_data, (rows, cols)), shape=(n, n)).tocsr()\n    C = D.copy()\n    C.data[:] = 1.0  # binary connectivities\n    return C, D\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
