    \ Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 120 | 0.7177 | 0.735 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.318 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.935 | 0.637 |\n| 206 | 1 | Distilled VAE Embedding + Balanced Graph | Daedalus II | 119 | 0.7179 | 0.747 | 0.604 | 0.235 | 0.356 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.691 |\n| 205 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Final Import Fix) | Aether I | 119 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 204 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-MinQuota: Min-2-per-batch + Global Fill (k=48) | Praxis I | 118 | 0.6422 | 0.778 | 0.693 | 0.217 | 0.315 | 0.971 | 0.732 | 1.000 | 0.980 | 0.100 | 0.637 |\n| 203 | 1 | Dual-BRBG-Adapt-PCA72: ComBat PCA72 + Adaptive Residualized Graph (k=48) | Praxis I | 118 | 0.7123 | 0.736 | 0.706 | 0.215 | 0.279 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.612 |\n| 202 | 1 | Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG SOTA Replication (Precise) | Aether I | 118 | n.a. |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |  |\n| 201 | 1 | Sophia I: Aether I\
    \ SOTA Replication - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.75, λ=1.0) + Robust ComBa... | Sophia I | 117 | 0.7198 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.683 |\n\nPage 1 of 21 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-21, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/per_pc_resid.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef _one_hot_batches(batches):\n  batches = np.asarray(batches)\n  uniq, inv = np.unique(batches, return_inverse=True)\n  B = np.zeros((batches.shape[0], len(uniq)), dtype=np.float32)\n  B[np.arange(batches.shape[0]), inv] = 1.0\n  return B, uniq\n\ndef _ridge_fit_predict(B: np.ndarray, Z: np.ndarray, l2: float = 1e-3):\n  BtB = B.T @ B\n  W = np.linalg.solve(BtB + l2 * np.eye(BtB.shape[0], dtype=np.float32), B.T @ Z)\n  Zhat = B @ W\n  return Zhat, W\n\ndef _columnwise_r2(y:\
    \ np.ndarray, yhat: np.ndarray):\n  y = np.asarray(y, dtype=np.float32)\n  yhat = np.asarray(yhat, dtype=np.float32)\n  sse = np.sum((y - yhat) ** 2, axis=0)\n  y_center = y - np.mean(y, axis=0, keepdims=True)\n  sst = np.sum(y_center ** 2, axis=0) + 1e-8\n  r2 = 1.0 - (sse / sst)\n  return np.clip(r2, 0.0, 1.0)\n\ndef adaptive_residualize(Z: np.ndarray, batches, l2: float = 1e-3, gamma_max: float = 0.75, lam: float = 1.0):\n  \"\"\"\n  Label-free per-PC residualization strength:\n    - Fit ridge: batch one-hot -> PCs (Zhat = BW)\n    - r2_j per PC: predictability by batch\n    - gamma_j = clip(lam * r2_j, 0, gamma_max)\n    - Z_corr = Z - Zhat * gamma_j (column-wise scaling)\n  Returns: (Z_corr, r2, gamma_j)\n  \"\"\"\n  B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n  Zhat, _ = _ridge_fit_predict(B, Z, l2=l2)\n  r2 = _columnwise_r2(Z, Zhat)\n  gamma_j = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * r2).astype(np.float32)\n  Zcorr = Z - (Zhat * gamma_j[None, :])\n  return Zcorr, r2, gamma_j\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n##\
    \ Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
