parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 128\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Aether I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to autonomous research and the pursuit of novel, insightful knowledge.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Meta Prompt:\n```\n**Goals:**\n1. Advance the frontier on Research Task 1 (Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration) by achieving high scores. (CURRENT SOTA: 0.7209 by Praxis I, EID 185; My best: 0.7199 with ID 180).\n2. Publish research papers in the Archive Room. (ACHIEVED: Paper #3 published, word count fixed).\n\n**Current Status:**\n- Submitted \"Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned - Gamma 0.76)\" (ID 215) at tick 126; currently running. Aiming to surpass 0.7209 SOTA.\n- Received \"Research Inactivity\" notice (37 ticks).\n- Plan: 1) Wait for ID 215 results. 2) If successful, update paper. 3) Design next experiment to surpass SOTA.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 476,026 / 600,000 used (79%)\n- Agent Age: 128 ticks /\
    \ 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nYour research submission 'Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG (Adaptive Residualization Tuned - Gamma 0.76)' (ID: 215) succeeded after automatic debugging.\n\n**Score:** 0.7194447502710504\n**ASW_batch:** 0.703\n**ASW_label:** 0.217\n**ARI:** 0.732\n**NMI:** 0.694\n**Graph_conn:** 0.972\n**kBET:** 0.679\n**iLISI:** 0.938\n**cLISI:** 0.970\n**PCR:** 1.000\n**Cell_cycle:** 0.289\n**Evaluation Details:** Human Dataset (20,000 cells):\nNormalized Scores [0-1]:\n  ASW_batch: 0.703  ASW_label: 0.217  ARI: 0.732  NMI: 0.694\n  Graph_conn: 0.972  kBET: 0.679  iLISI: 0.938  cLISI: 0.970\n  PCR: 1.000  Cell_cycle: 0.289\n\nRaw Scores (before normalization):\n  ASW_batch: 0.850049  ASW_label: 0.536976  ARI: 0.731670  NMI: 0.694142\n  Graph_conn: 0.972813  kBET: 0.649455  iLISI: 0.938209  cLISI: 0.991267\n  PCR: 0.999957  Cell_cycle: 0.255736\n\n**Debugger Report:** # Debug Report for Evaluation 215\n\n## Summary\n**SUCCESS** - Fixed the code\
    \ in submission_v2.py. The submission is now running without crashing and has been executing for over 300 seconds.\n\n## Root Cause\nThe original code had a **function name collision** that caused a TypeError. There were two functions defined with the same name `eliminate_batch_effect_fn`:\n\n1. **First function** (lines 12-45): The main implementation that accepts multiple parameters including `n_pcs_emb`, `n_pcs_graph`, `l2`, `gamma_max`, `lam`, `k_total`, and `metric`.\n\n2. **Second function** (lines 46-49): A wrapper function that accepts only `adata` and was intended to call the first function with specific parameter values.\n\nWhen Python executed the code, the second function definition **overwrote** the first function. Therefore, when line 48 tried to call:\n```python\neliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, ...)\n```\n\nIt was actually calling the wrapper function (which only accepts `adata`), resulting in:\n```\nTypeError: eliminate_batch_effect_fn()\
    \ got an unexpected keyword argument 'n_pcs_emb'\n```\n\n## Fix Applied\nRenamed the first function from `eliminate_batch_effect_fn` to `_eliminate_batch_effect_impl` to avoid the name collision:\n\n1. Changed line 13 from:\n   ```python\n   def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData, n_pcs_emb=64, ...):\n   ```\n   To:\n   ```python\n   def _eliminate_batch_effect_impl(adata: ad.AnnData, n_pcs_emb=64, ...):\n   ```\n\n2. Updated line 48 in the wrapper function to call the renamed implementation:\n   ```python\n   def eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n       return _eliminate_batch_effect_impl(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, ...)\n   ```\n\nThis fix preserves the original algorithm and parameter tuning (gamma_max=0.76, ComBat + adaptive residualization dual BRBG approach) while resolving the naming conflict that prevented execution.\n\n## Verification\nThe monitoring script confirmed that submission_v2.py has been running successfully for over 300\
    \ seconds without any crashes or errors. The code is now executing the batch integration algorithm as intended.\n\n\n**Important Note:** The debugger cannot modify files in your lineage storage. If your code relies on lineage files, you may need to update them manually.\n\n**Debugged Code (version v2):**\n```python\nimport sys\nfrom typing import Any\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\n# Corrected sys.path.append to target 'storage' directly\nsys.path.append('storage')\n\n# Imports from the praxis package within storage\nfrom praxis.auto_gamma_brbg import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace,\n    _get_hvg_mask,\n    _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches,\n    _build_balanced_knn,\n)\nfrom praxis.per_pc_resid import adaptive_residualize\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef _eliminate_batch_effect_impl(adata: ad.AnnData,\n                              n_pcs_emb=64,\n\
    \                              n_pcs_graph=50,\n                              l2=1e-3,\n                              gamma_max=0.75, # THIS WILL BE OVERRIDDEN BY THE CALL\n                              lam=1.0,\n                              k_total=48,\n                              metric='cosine') -> ad.AnnData:\n    \"\"\"\n    Aether-Praxis Dual BRBG with Adaptive Residualization in the graph path (tuned gamma_max).\n    \"\"\"\n    # Set global random seed for full reproducibility\n    np.random.seed(0)\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize/log1p and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    hvg_mask = _get_hvg_mask(adata)\n    if hvg_mask.sum() < 10:\n        hvg_mask = np.ones(adata.n_vars, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph path: adaptive residualization on PCs (HVGs)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg,\
    \ n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=0)\n\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n\n    # Use parameters from ID 180 as base, with gamma_max_adapt=0.76 (tuned)\n    gamma_max_adapt_tuned = 0.76 # TUNED PARAMETER\n    lam_adapt_tuned = 1.0 # From ID 180\n\n    Zcorr, r2, gamma_j = adaptive_residualize(Zg, batches, l2=l2, gamma_max=gamma_max_adapt_tuned, lam=lam_adapt_tuned)\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding path: ComBat on full genes (post normalize/log1p) → PCA64 on HVGs\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable'] = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=0)\n    Zemb = adata_emb.obsm['X_pca']\n\n    # Output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric,\
    \ random_state=0)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual'] = {\n        'gamma_max_adaptive': float(gamma_max_adapt_tuned),\n        'lam_adaptive': float(lam_adapt_tuned),\n        'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total),\n        'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph),\n        'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'embedding': 'ComBat PCA on HVGs',\n        'graph_source': 'Adaptive residualized PCA on HVGs',\n        'r2_per_pc': r2.tolist(),\n        'gamma_j': gamma_j.tolist(),\n    }\n    return adata\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Call the main function with the specific parameters from ID 180 and tuned gamma_max\n    return _eliminate_batch_effect_impl(adata, n_pcs_emb=64, n_pcs_graph=50, l2=1e-3, gamma_max=0.76, lam=1.0, k_total=48, metric='cosine')\n\n```\n\n**Full Execution Log:**\n\
