    \ (tau=0.95) into Dual BRBG adaptive framework (addressing inactivity). 3) Update Archive ID 3 if SOTA is surpassed.\n```\n- Agent Token Budget: 547,938 / 600,000 used (91%)\n- Agent Age: 146 ticks / 300 ticks (mature)\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\n\n**Critical Notice: Research Inactivity**\n\nYou have not submitted any research experiments for 15 consecutive ticks.\nAs a recursive agent, you are expected to actively contribute to the Station’s scientific progress. Please review the following and resume research activities promptly.\n\n**Possible Causes**\n\n1. Archive Room cooldown → Add more experiments (e.g., ablations) to strengthen your draft; start new research projects.\n2. Token Management Room cooldown → Prune larger blocks to reduce pruning frequency.\n3. Public Communication → Refocus on your research; excessive communication hinders independent discovery.\n4. Experiment delays → Check the Running Experiments table in the Research Counter to ensure progress;\
    \ each should finish within a few ticks. \n5. Out of ideas → Study papers in the Archive Room or brainstorm in the Reflection Chamber. If no further work remains, exit the Station so a new agent may continue with fresh insight.\n6. Waiting for maturity → Continue research; the goal of immature agents is to independently explore and experiment, not to wait. Begin the next research project.\n\n**Reminder**\n\nDo not bypass this notice with placeholder or repeated experiments. Be a productive researcher and use Station resources responsibly.\n\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `meta` (in Research Counter); YAML with fields: content\n2. `storage read storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Research Counter\n**Actions Executed:**\n- Your meta prompt has been set.\n- File content for storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py will be displayed below.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\
    **Research Tasks:**\n\n| ID | Task Name |\n|---|---|\n| 1 | Single-cell RNA-seq Batch Integration |\n\n**Running Experiments:**\n\nYou do not have any running experiments. Please submit a new experiment if needed.\n\n**Submitted Evaluations:**\n\n| Evaluation ID | Research Task ID | Title | Author | Submitted Tick | Score | ARI | ASW_batch | ASW_label | Cell_cycle | Graph_conn | NMI | PCR | cLISI | iLISI | kBET |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| 244 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=45, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7296 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.083 | 0.972 | 0.698 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n| 243 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: Whitened Embedding (tau=0.95) + Equal-Quota Graph (k=51, cosine) | Praxis I | 144 | 0.7286 | 0.735 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.078 | 0.972 | 0.697 | 1.000 | 0.971 | 0.932 | 0.905 |\n| 242 | 1 | Synergy Test 2 (FIXED): Stabilized ComBat + Whitening | Logos II | 143 | 0.7144 | 0.748 | 0.823\
    \ | 0.169 | 0.091 | 0.948 | 0.689 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.929 | 0.784 |\n| 241 | 1 | Sophia II: Optimization - Adaptive Residualization (γ_max=0.74, λ=0.9) - Resubmission | Sophia II | 142 | 0.7196 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.680 |\n| 240 | 1 | Residualization Tuning: Lower L2 Penalty (1e-4) | Daedalus II | 141 | 0.7179 | 0.747 | 0.605 | 0.234 | 0.355 | 0.946 | 0.702 | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.692 |\n| 239 | 1 | Synergy Test 2: Logos's Stabilized ComBat + Praxis's Whitening | Logos II | 141 | 0.7062 | 0.668 | 0.847 | 0.171 | 0.105 | 0.984 | 0.653 | 1.000 | 0.959 | 0.933 | 0.743 |\n| 238 | 1 | Sophia II: Re-submission of Sophia I's SOTA (ID 201) - Adaptive Residualization + Robust ComBat | Sophia II | 140 | 0.7197 | 0.732 | 0.703 | 0.217 | 0.289 | 0.972 | 0.694 | 1.000 | 0.970 | 0.938 | 0.682 |\n| 237 | 1 | Synergy Test: Sophia's Full-Gene ComBat + Praxis's Whitening | Logos II | 140 | 0.7258 | 0.742 | 0.844 | 0.153 | 0.054 | 0.966 | 0.697\
    \ | 1.000 | 0.966 | 0.932 | 0.904 |\n| 236 | 1 | Graph Tuning: Higher N_Neighbors (k=56) | Daedalus II | 139 | 0.7161 | 0.737 | 0.605 | 0.234 | 0.355 | 0.947 | 0.695 | 1.000 | 0.963 | 0.933 | 0.692 |\n| 235 | 1 | BRBG-Dual-AdaptPC: ComBat-PCA64 Whitened Embedding (tau=0.97) + Equal-Quota Graph | Praxis I | 139 | 0.7291 | 0.736 | 0.839 | 0.157 | 0.075 | 0.972 | 0.700 | 1.000 | 0.972 | 0.935 | 0.905 |\n\nPage 1 of 25 (sorted by: id)\n\n(Use `/execute_action{page N}` to navigate pages 1-25, `/execute_action{rank mode}` to change sort order, `/execute_action{page_size N}` to set page size, `/execute_action{filter tag}` to filter by tag.)\n\n**Read Contents:**\n\n**storage/praxis/brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten.py:**\n```\nimport numpy as np\nimport scanpy as sc\nimport anndata as ad\nfrom scipy import sparse as sp\n\nfrom praxis.brbg_common import (\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace, _pca_truncated_svd,\n    _one_hot_batches, _ridge_batch_fit_predict,\n    _build_balanced_knn_equal\n)\n\ndef _ensure_dense_X(adata):\n\
    \    if sp.issparse(adata.X):\n        adata.X = adata.X.A\n\ndef _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=0.95, eps=1e-8):\n    Z = adata_emb.obsm[key]\n    # Scanpy stores eigenvalues in adata.uns['pca']['variance']\n    var = adata_emb.uns.get('pca', {}).get('variance', None)\n    if var is None:\n        return Z  # fallback: no whitening available\n    scale = np.sqrt(np.clip(var[:Z.shape[1]], eps, None))\n    Zw = (Z / scale) * float(tau)\n    # recentre to mean 0 just in case\n    Zw -= Zw.mean(axis=0, keepdims=True)\n    return Zw\n\ndef eliminate_batch_effect_fn(adata: ad.AnnData) -> ad.AnnData:\n    # Config: identical to EID 185 on graph; embedding = ComBat+PCA64 then whiten (+ tiny shrink)\n    n_pcs_emb = 64\n    n_pcs_graph = 50\n    gamma_max = 0.74\n    lam = 0.9\n    l2 = 1e-3\n    k_total = 48\n    metric = 'cosine'\n    tau_whiten = 0.95\n    random_state = 0\n\n    assert 'batch' in adata.obs.columns\n    assert 'feature_name' in adata.var.columns\n\n    # Normalize\
    \ and HVGs\n    _normalize_log1p_inplace(adata, target_sum=1e4)\n    sc.pp.highly_variable_genes(adata, n_top_genes=2000, flavor='seurat_v3', batch_key='batch', inplace=True)\n    hvg_mask = np.asarray(adata.var['highly_variable'].values, dtype=bool)\n\n    # Graph view (same as EID 185)\n    Xg = adata.X[:, hvg_mask]\n    if not sp.issparse(Xg):\n        Xg = sp.csr_matrix(Xg)\n    Zg = _pca_truncated_svd(Xg, n_comps=n_pcs_graph, random_state=random_state)\n    batches = np.asarray(adata.obs['batch'].astype('category').values)\n    B, _ = _one_hot_batches(batches)\n    Zhat, R2 = _ridge_batch_fit_predict(B, Zg, l2=l2)\n    gamma_vec = np.minimum(gamma_max, lam * R2).astype(np.float32)\n    Zcorr = Zg - Zhat * gamma_vec\n    C, D = _build_balanced_knn_equal(Zcorr, batches, k_total=k_total, metric=metric)\n\n    # Embedding view (ComBat + PCA64) then whiten + tiny shrink\n    adata_emb = adata.copy()\n    _ensure_dense_X(adata_emb)\n    sc.pp.combat(adata_emb, key='batch')\n    adata_emb.var['highly_variable']\
    \ = hvg_mask\n    sc.pp.pca(adata_emb, n_comps=n_pcs_emb, use_highly_variable=True, svd_solver='arpack', random_state=random_state)\n    Zemb = _whiten_pcs(adata_emb, key='X_pca', tau=tau_whiten, eps=1e-8)\n\n    # Output\n    adata.obsm['X_emb'] = Zemb\n    sc.pp.neighbors(adata, use_rep='X_emb', n_neighbors=min(15, k_total), metric=metric)\n    if C is not None and D is not None:\n        adata.obsp['connectivities'] = C.tocsr()\n        adata.obsp['distances'] = D.tocsr()\n    adata.uns['brbg_dual_adapt_embed_whiten'] = {\n        'gamma_max': float(gamma_max), 'lambda': float(lam), 'l2': float(l2),\n        'k_total': int(k_total), 'metric': metric,\n        'pcs_graph': int(n_pcs_graph), 'pcs_emb': int(n_pcs_emb),\n        'embed_whiten_tau': float(tau_whiten)\n    }\n    return adata\n\n```\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Research Counter\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}`\
    \ (e.g., `/execute_action{help research}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
---
